{"us-male\u0001Como membro da Diretoria, o seu inglês precisa carregar visão , não só informação. Esta primeira aula constrói a linguagem da estratégia: onde estamos, para onde vamos e como chegar lá. Três movimentos executivos: declarar a vision (o destino), definir o horizon (3–5 anos) e conectar as decisões de hoje a essa meta de longo prazo. Líderes que falam assim soam críveis em qualquer board.":"audio/3de74944071a23dd.mp3","us-male\u0001Our vision is to be the partner of choice for mission-critical construction in Latin America. Over the next five years, we're doubling down on data centers and healthcare, where demand is structural. Every decision we make today is measured against that horizon.":"audio/2b188fcdd7e451ae.mp3","us-male\u0001Qual é a sua visão real de cinco anos para a Racional — e o que você pararia de fazer para chegar lá? Responda em inglês (pode apoiar em português no que travar).":"audio/2918c558846977b5.mp3","us-male\u0001vision. Our vision is to lead the market.":"audio/e292a1cc407f6a56.mp3","us-male\u0001long-term. This is a long-term play.":"audio/17c4f9eb5b1b68e9.mp3","us-male\u0001strategy. Our strategy is clear.":"audio/8fb5ff7520345873.mp3","us-male\u0001horizon. We plan on a five-year horizon.":"audio/cdccb72aac7160b5.mp3","us-male\u0001partner of choice. We aim to be the partner of choice.":"audio/7af6dd21352497dd.mp3","us-male\u0001to double down on. We're doubling down on data centers.":"audio/9eafc932e634f0d7.mp3","us-male\u0001structural demand. The demand here is structural.":"audio/75869236e05c216d.mp3","us-male\u0001to position. We position ourselves as premium.":"audio/7b1c68014632921c.mp3","us-male\u0001competitive edge. Pre-construction is our competitive edge.":"audio/0ba2be26fda81fce.mp3","us-male\u0001to scale. We're ready to scale.":"audio/3c2484505693a20c.mp3","us-male\u0001value proposition. Our value proposition is delivery certainty.":"audio/e4f8d5d64db92c23.mp3","us-male\u0001to measure against. Every call is measured against the vision.":"audio/90efa0cae089454b.mp3","us-male\u0001milestone. Year three is a key milestone.":"audio/d93c5a3b35510032.mp3","us-male\u0001to allocate capital. We allocate capital to growth segments.":"audio/105e5b43986d5724.mp3","us-male\u0001sustainable growth. We're after sustainable growth.":"audio/80124a3aa20f1c9f.mp3","us-male\u0001Eu declaro uma visão estratégica clara em inglês.":"audio/8a206a17a13f6bb5.mp3","us-male\u0001Eu defino um horizonte de longo prazo (três a cinco anos).":"audio/81891142ad1650bc.mp3","us-male\u0001Eu uso vocabulário executivo: value proposition, competitive edge, allocate capital.":"audio/2041362939b35d2b.mp3","us-male\u0001Eu conecto as decisões de hoje à meta de longo prazo.":"audio/6befc88915f02a39.mp3","us-male\u0001I'm gonna grab a coffee, and then we can talk.":"audio/a2cbe1a79d902600.mp3","us-male\u0001São dois tempos verbais que você usa o tempo todo, mas que costumam se confundir na hora de falar. Present Simple = rotina, fato, cargo. \"I oversee the data center projects.\" (sempre, é o meu papel). Present Continuous = o que está acontecendo agora, temporário. \"Right now, we are building three data centers.\" Regra de ouro: na 3ª pessoa do Present Simple (he/she/it), o verbo ganha -s (oversees, runs, reports). No Continuous, é sempre am/is/are + verbo-ing .":"audio/253575fb83309b97.mp3","us-male\u0001Hello everyone, I'm Fábio Viccari, Director of Operations at Racional. I oversee our data center projects in Brazil. Right now, we are building three hyperscale sites and we are hiring two new commissioning teams.":"audio/09b2ed464f86ad74.mp3","us-male\u0001Em 15 segundos, como você se apresentaria a um novo executivo da Microsoft? Diga em voz alta — sem texto na frente.":"audio/7245917ff976ed94.mp3","us-male\u0001to oversee. I oversee the data center projects.":"audio/00967ac7329ff2a8.mp3","us-male\u0001to be responsible for. I am responsible for operations.":"audio/5a524276a79ab3fd.mp3","us-male\u0001to report to. I report to the board.":"audio/60ac325c091e2078.mp3","us-male\u0001currently. We are currently building three sites.":"audio/2e865a4f7d0bab61.mp3","us-male\u0001usually. I usually meet the client once a month.":"audio/f71216c4e9ac0924.mp3","us-male\u0001deliverable. The main deliverable is the energized building.":"audio/fcee40f89876fd89.mp3","us-male\u0001stakeholder. Every stakeholder joins the monthly call.":"audio/9cd7f57d9b2b97df.mp3","us-male\u0001schedule. The schedule is tight this quarter.":"audio/290f97f007f7c562.mp3","us-male\u0001scope. The scope includes design and construction.":"audio/435fc0c79d2df0fe.mp3","us-male\u0001to handle. I handle the relationship with big clients.":"audio/0929694896a67ad8.mp3","us-male\u0001on track. The project is on track.":"audio/07c44905c970afdc.mp3","us-male\u0001headquarters. Their headquarters are in Redmond.":"audio/678d4b4d8587e634.mp3","us-male\u0001to run a meeting. I run the monthly review.":"audio/48939186a9bc3860.mp3","us-male\u0001figures. I present the figures every month.":"audio/742efa8a9158b512.mp3","us-male\u0001role. My role is Director of Operations.":"audio/1a8e2559ca8d7a98.mp3","us-male\u0001I can introduce my role using the present simple.":"audio/633efac3b163c45d.mp3","us-male\u0001I can describe a project in progress using the present continuous.":"audio/9eac76b550b9ae21.mp3","us-male\u0001I know when to use 'usually' versus 'right now'.":"audio/ddc718be65aa668d.mp3","us-male\u0001I can open a monthly call with a confident two-sentence intro.":"audio/b09622eb9b618aba.mp3","us-male\u0001Hoje é a obra, não a planta. Você vai conversar . O foco é abrir a relação: cumprimentar, apresentar-se, apresentar a Racional em uma frase e devolver a palavra com uma pergunta. Estrutura de abertura que sempre funciona: Greeting → Name & role → One line about Racional → Question back.":"audio/ef58eee980d5bad7.mp3","us-male\u0001Good morning! It's a pleasure to finally meet you. I'm Fábio, Director of Operations at Racional — we build mission-critical projects like data centers. How has your week been so far?":"audio/fb868ab48b2a423c.mp3","us-male\u0001Pense em um cliente real seu (Microsoft, AWS ou Google). Como você abriria a próxima reunião com ele em inglês? Fale.":"audio/5d5a1b86c2d34f2d.mp3","us-male\u0001It's a pleasure to meet you. It's a pleasure to meet you in person.":"audio/6662d4ae4f0684e9.mp3","us-male\u0001to finally meet. Great to finally meet you.":"audio/a54b1e486912b4b0.mp3","us-male\u0001mission-critical. We build mission-critical projects.":"audio/ad377ba8769757e9.mp3","us-male\u0001How has your week been?. How has your week been so far?":"audio/c4905cd40f3a6233.mp3","us-male\u0001to look forward to. I look forward to working with you.":"audio/400517023fda391f.mp3","us-male\u0001on behalf of. On behalf of Racional, welcome.":"audio/4ea9dc4e6a43e692.mp3","us-male\u0001to walk you through. Let me walk you through our team.":"audio/4ba42d83143cb396.mp3","us-male\u0001counterpart. You'll be my main counterpart.":"audio/366f4b9d9349513f.mp3","us-male\u0001to be based in. We are based in São Paulo.":"audio/0df5265e8b66b180.mp3","us-male\u0001to take care of. My team takes care of delivery.":"audio/bedff56ef5d629c1.mp3","us-male\u0001shall we. Shall we start with introductions?":"audio/ca6b66441e710df4.mp3","us-male\u0001agenda. Let's look at today's agenda.":"audio/c01a082847c7e8ea.mp3","us-male\u0001to kick off. Let's kick off the meeting.":"audio/030ce3ae6d83b6b0.mp3","us-male\u0001glad. I'm glad you could join.":"audio/6e240564107d8a02.mp3","us-male\u0001to break the ice. A little small talk breaks the ice.":"audio/aec9207d07cc4d95.mp3","us-male\u0001I can open a first meeting warmly and professionally.":"audio/df1f73ec997a43a4.mp3","us-male\u0001I can present Racional in a single strong sentence.":"audio/139a870470a48496.mp3","us-male\u0001I can hand the floor back with a natural question.":"audio/7f5133a5faa0e58d.mp3","us-male\u0001I can act as the host and propose the next step.":"audio/5ec7473dd74f4e8d.mp3","us-male\u0001Y'all have a great day now — we'll talk real soon.":"audio/fbd0a3cba2c412cd.mp3","us-male\u0001Quem pergunta conduz a reunião. As WH-questions abrem informação: What, Where, When, Who, Why, How, How much, How long. As question tags confirmam: \"The schedule is tight, isn't it?\" E as estruturas de clarificação salvam você quando não entendeu: \"Sorry, could you say that again?\"":"audio/c520be19070f72e0.mp3","us-male\u0001Sorry, could you repeat the last part? Just to make sure I understand: you need the report by Friday, is that right? And how long will the review take on your side?":"audio/a728d67ba5b17309.mp3","us-male\u0001Qual pergunta você mais esquece de fazer nas suas reuniões — e que evitaria um mal-entendido? Diga em inglês como você faria essa pergunta.":"audio/fed50f7d29d64fe7.mp3","us-male\u0001What. What is the deadline?":"audio/1dc0fc9857dba197.mp3","us-male\u0001When. When does it start?":"audio/7b675df43f62b256.mp3","us-male\u0001How long. How long will it take?":"audio/45c616e6cf1a71c0.mp3","us-male\u0001How much. How much does it cost?":"audio/e7815f7eaccbbaab.mp3","us-male\u0001Why. Why is the schedule tight?":"audio/627b5f67dc6314ef.mp3","us-male\u0001isn't it?. The scope is clear, isn't it?":"audio/7d3444a5c99c0607.mp3","us-male\u0001right?. We meet on Friday, right?":"audio/8ac826096b8f647e.mp3","us-male\u0001Could you repeat?. Sorry, could you repeat that?":"audio/4e6ffd29739e8959.mp3","us-male\u0001Just to make sure. Just to make sure I understand…":"audio/8cb4c948e998b5bc.mp3","us-male\u0001to clarify. Let me clarify one point.":"audio/6086bf1fca4dd83c.mp3","us-male\u0001Do you mean…?. Do you mean next week?":"audio/2ae981a09aa304d6.mp3","us-male\u0001in other words. In other words, we are on track.":"audio/e5b5cf04d60a2830.mp3","us-male\u0001to follow. Sorry, I didn't follow.":"audio/7b3d89ec418e82ad.mp3","us-male\u0001Could you slow down?. Could you slow down a bit?":"audio/d162963a00d22d52.mp3","us-male\u0001to rephrase. Let me rephrase the question.":"audio/1c81ee1c6a1a4925.mp3","us-male\u0001I can ask WH-questions to open up information.":"audio/9b1eecabbe39f764.mp3","us-male\u0001I can confirm with a question tag (…isn't it?).":"audio/d42c4cd3e0363aee.mp3","us-male\u0001I can ask someone to repeat or slow down politely.":"audio/1ba909e4743a3180.mp3","us-male\u0001I can clarify before acting, to avoid rework.":"audio/f05ace5724fe9916.mp3","us-female\u0001It's gonna be, like, a really good project, you know?":"audio/106adfdd4ca4f789.mp3","us-female\u0001Vamos começar pelo começo — e pelo mais importante: abrir a boca . Em inglês, cumprimentar é quase automático, e dominar isso já te dá confiança nos 10 primeiros segundos de qualquer reunião. Good morning = de manhã. Good afternoon = depois do meio-dia. Good evening = à noite. Hi / Hello = qualquer hora, mais informal — perfeito para o pessoal do Google, que costuma ser descontraído. Não se preocupe com perfeição. Se sair \"Good morning\" às 2 da tarde, o mundo não acaba. O importante é cumprimentar.":"audio/58ed1dee53241f03.mp3","us-female\u0001Good morning, everyone! It's great to see you. Hi, I'm from Racional. Welcome — let's start.":"audio/cd973480fed6fde8.mp3","us-female\u0001Pense na sua próxima reunião com o Google. Que horas costuma ser? Cumprimente em voz alta como você abriria essa reunião.":"audio/507760591085dea3.mp3","us-female\u0001good morning. Good morning! Welcome to the meeting.":"audio/657cc165c0f189d6.mp3","us-female\u0001good afternoon. Good afternoon, everyone.":"audio/c2dfe53fd5a3bf78.mp3","us-female\u0001good evening. Good evening, thank you for joining.":"audio/e73a6e032dc89d13.mp3","us-female\u0001hi. Hi! Good to see you.":"audio/6a83c21fdc18e3a9.mp3","us-female\u0001hello. Hello, I'm from Racional.":"audio/b4378937d94f992c.mp3","us-female\u0001everyone. Good morning, everyone!":"audio/e1437efb6fcd06af.mp3","us-female\u0001it's great to see you. It's great to see you again.":"audio/acf514e3f49489f2.mp3","us-female\u0001welcome. Welcome to São Paulo.":"audio/dfe62a8488c005d4.mp3","us-female\u0001thank you for joining. Thank you for joining us today.":"audio/34c2094c497b310a.mp3","us-female\u0001how are you?. Hi, how are you?":"audio/36dc2429e08fb33e.mp3","us-female\u0001I'm fine, thanks. I'm fine, thanks. And you?":"audio/25925b35f62e74ac.mp3","us-female\u0001nice to see you again. Nice to see you again.":"audio/edda7f6dccfbe2d2.mp3","us-female\u0001let's start. Welcome — let's start.":"audio/662ef39ffbc6db27.mp3","us-female\u0001good to be here. It's good to be here.":"audio/393bc83ff7c95340.mp3","us-female\u0001shall we begin?. Everyone's here — shall we begin?":"audio/35333bce3cb46a31.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu consigo cumprimentar certo em qualquer horário (morning / afternoon / evening).":"audio/e4c4be3c1bdf3629.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu sei abrir informal com 'Hi' e 'Hello'.":"audio/8415a275c378ca9f.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu consigo dizer 'Welcome — let's start' para abrir a reunião.":"audio/26f446af62dc331e.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu falei em voz alta sem travar — fluência é isso.":"audio/ef73f712ee5b59c8.mp3","us-female\u0001Número é a coisa que mais trava brasileiro em reunião. E em negociação, número é tudo. Hoje a meta é simples: dizer 0 a 10 em voz alta, rápido e claro . Cuidado com dois clássicos: three (o \"th\" é com a língua entre os dentes, não é \"tree\") e zero (que em telefone/contagem também vira \"oh\"). Drill é repetição. Quanto mais você repetir hoje, mais automático fica.":"audio/ac99497ce6268b16.mp3","us-female\u0001We have three teams on site, two more arriving next week. Building four is at level seven. Zero accidents this month.":"audio/2ea2c18d3c6ffe80.mp3","us-female\u0001Quantas equipes, prédios ou meses tem o seu projeto atual com o Google? Diga os números em voz alta, em inglês.":"audio/56b227caa4bb6b01.mp3","us-female\u0001zero. Zero accidents this month.":"audio/c128147718ef70dc.mp3","us-female\u0001one. We need one more crane.":"audio/5176b693a35e932d.mp3","us-female\u0001two. Two teams are on site.":"audio/d4e7f677ab7e55d0.mp3","us-female\u0001three. Three buildings are ready.":"audio/4e9f40637cbaaa8c.mp3","us-female\u0001four. Building four is delayed.":"audio/f14007a5fbe3e2ae.mp3","us-female\u0001five. Five days to the deadline.":"audio/adc2033ab7cd9f93.mp3","us-female\u0001six. Six inspections passed.":"audio/85c2ba131cf47814.mp3","us-female\u0001seven. Level seven is done.":"audio/d3233daf5d180aec.mp3","us-female\u0001eight. Eight hours per shift.":"audio/fd3984ef25b49c9b.mp3","us-female\u0001nine. Nine months to handover.":"audio/768c1a6e480380d7.mp3","us-female\u0001ten. Ten teams in total.":"audio/cb52c3d74db6e635.mp3","us-female\u0001how many?. How many teams do you have?":"audio/cfbdc23e56bc8270.mp3","us-female\u0001a couple. A couple of weeks.":"audio/952f5b36f701fc50.mp3","us-female\u0001in total. Ten teams in total.":"audio/32dbbb723586485e.mp3","us-female\u0001on site. Three teams on site.":"audio/6171ee5f4d25b365.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu digo de 0 a 10 em inglês em voz alta, sem travar.":"audio/b2d8640f98ff456d.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu acerto o som difícil de 'three' e 'nine'.":"audio/7a5b45de5b82a1f1.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu respondo 'How many?' com um número na hora.":"audio/49968f7df8fec8e1.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu uso número + contexto para soar no controle da obra.":"audio/da2b1213695fe69e.mp3","us-female\u0001O Google é cliente de data center. Se você entende o que é um data center em inglês, você fala a língua do cliente — e isso constrói confiança. Data center = um prédio cheio de servidores que guardam e processam dados. Pense num \"cérebro\" gigante da internet. O Google constrói data centers para rodar buscas, e-mails, vídeos e, hoje, inteligência artificial. Hoje o foco é só o essencial: 15 palavras que abrem a porta do mundo técnico.":"audio/42e6be27a5f02bf3.mp3","us-female\u0001This is a data center. Inside, we have thousands of servers. They store and process data. The building needs a lot of power and strong cooling to keep the servers safe.":"audio/84d5dee7712692d5.mp3","us-female\u0001Com suas palavras, em inglês: por que o Google precisa de tantos data centers hoje? Fale, mesmo que em frases curtas.":"audio/99537b689e8217ec.mp3","us-female\u0001data center. This is a data center.":"audio/45e3a72ea55a30f7.mp3","us-female\u0001server. We have thousands of servers.":"audio/469c30eece0a11df.mp3","us-female\u0001data. Servers store and process data.":"audio/2ebd39ec72987b1f.mp3","us-female\u0001to store. Servers store data.":"audio/37874f1d9f98ff06.mp3","us-female\u0001to process. They process millions of requests.":"audio/9e889aede5cf5031.mp3","us-female\u0001power. The building needs a lot of power.":"audio/e5b24bd633726570.mp3","us-female\u0001cooling. Strong cooling keeps the servers safe.":"audio/bc70bcabe4bc53b9.mp3","us-female\u0001building. The building is huge.":"audio/b3721704d7431d2d.mp3","us-female\u0001rack. Each rack holds many servers.":"audio/c3e552dd22e7f235.mp3","us-female\u0001the cloud. Your photos live in the cloud.":"audio/073a859b9aceb9a0.mp3","us-female\u0001to run. Data centers run the internet.":"audio/03e0fb958ed6942b.mp3","us-female\u0001huge. It's a huge facility.":"audio/eb4efec83461afb7.mp3","us-female\u0001facility. This facility never stops.":"audio/85678c6fcb071941.mp3","us-female\u000124/7. A data center runs 24/7.":"audio/573a881383fa8dcb.mp3","us-female\u0001to keep safe. Cooling keeps the servers safe.":"audio/18e4e4c67f258135.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu sei dizer o que é um data center em inglês.":"audio/2654fa8cd02dcf8b.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu conheço as palavras server, data, power e cooling.":"audio/44a55f685b4b402a.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu explico, em frases simples, por que o Google constrói data centers.":"audio/b56001eacb995818.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu conduzo uma visita de obra falando a língua do cliente.":"audio/019f9be96e9d76fe.mp3","us-male\u0001Park the car and meet us at the site office.":"audio/55434be3534e00cc.mp3","gb-male\u0001Como gerente de contrato, você lidera coordenadores, gerentes de área e equipes. Falar como você lidera — o seu estilo — é uma forma poderosa de mostrar maturidade em inglês. Quatro estilos clássicos: directive (você decide, rápido — ótimo na crise), coaching (você desenvolve as pessoas), participative (você envolve o time) e delegative (você passa a responsabilidade). Os melhores gestores trocam de estilo conforme a situação na obra.":"audio/20ebaafd073764bc.mp3","gb-male\u0001On site, I adapt my style. In a crisis, I'm directive — I make the call fast. Day to day, I'm more participative: I bring the coordinators in before deciding. With junior engineers, I coach.":"audio/a8dc7d082b92d7ea.mp3","gb-male\u0001Pense na sua última semana difícil na obra. Que estilo de liderança você mais usou — e mudaria algo? Responda — pode misturar inglês e português.":"audio/df69024ad9827025.mp3","gb-male\u0001leadership style. My leadership style depends on the situation.":"audio/7a855f3594f1577b.mp3","gb-male\u0001directive. In a crisis, I'm directive.":"audio/582e755e380e21fe.mp3","gb-male\u0001to coach. I coach the junior engineers.":"audio/cd65e1acca72431f.mp3","gb-male\u0001participative. I'm participative in planning.":"audio/38082c63901fd481.mp3","gb-male\u0001to delegate. I delegate ownership to my coordinators.":"audio/91ba72238e048fa7.mp3","gb-male\u0001to make the call. Someone has to make the call.":"audio/1f340869edf09828.mp3","gb-male\u0001crew. The crew starts at 7 a.m.":"audio/a6b5d9f216926f76.mp3","gb-male\u0001coordinator. Each coordinator runs one front.":"audio/d3785be15feeb604.mp3","gb-male\u0001to lead by example. I lead by example on safety.":"audio/f355567fdc9bd97b.mp3","gb-male\u0001accountability. Accountability keeps the project on track.":"audio/c157953a97be5a20.mp3","gb-male\u0001to empower. I empower my team to decide.":"audio/43b3babdb84f71f7.mp3","gb-male\u0001hands-on. I'm a hands-on manager.":"audio/bd5bdb722db00954.mp3","gb-male\u0001to step in. I step in only when needed.":"audio/4dd78362080d593d.mp3","gb-male\u0001buy-in. I need the team's buy-in first.":"audio/0d09dd46311175dc.mp3","gb-male\u0001to adapt. I adapt my style to the moment.":"audio/c638d8ac58d3a3b3.mp3","gb-male\u0001Eu sei nomear os quatro estilos de liderança em inglês.":"audio/fe94f75310fde480.mp3","gb-male\u0001Eu combino o estilo certo com a situação na obra.":"audio/e246ea7c441f38fd.mp3","gb-male\u0001Eu descrevo o meu próprio estilo de liderança para um cliente.":"audio/eaff9f91e7f5b43a.mp3","gb-male\u0001Eu falo sobre dar autonomia e desenvolver o meu time.":"audio/7abc7147bb586141.mp3","gb-male\u0001Esta é uma aula BRIDGE — mais leve de propósito, para manter a energia entre os blocos técnicos pesados. E ela é construída em torno de algo que você ama: música . Música é um dos melhores criadores de rapport em negócios. Quase todo mundo tem um artista que adora. Hoje começamos pelo Seal — a lenda do soul britânico de Kiss from a Rose e Crazy — e pela linguagem de shows e concertos. Relaxe e aproveite. Falar do que você ama é o caminho mais rápido para a fluência.":"audio/13996c0cd483bbfc.mp3","gb-male\u0001I'm a huge Seal fan. His voice is unmistakable. I saw him live once and the whole crowd sang Kiss from a Rose — goosebumps. What kind of music are you into?":"audio/4c7aae88404dd911.mp3","gb-male\u0001Quem é o seu artista favorito e qual foi o melhor show que você já foi? Conte a história — pode misturar inglês e português, e divirta-se.":"audio/c933408a3c2fee4b.mp3","gb-male\u0001to be into (music). What music are you into?":"audio/48a1e6ad0cfff25a.mp3","gb-male\u0001a huge fan. I'm a huge Seal fan.":"audio/6ee389132d42ce48.mp3","gb-male\u0001soul (music). Seal blends soul and pop.":"audio/8aa2b3eb574f84eb.mp3","gb-male\u0001voice. His voice is unmistakable.":"audio/4e74a3527d06f7b9.mp3","gb-male\u0001unmistakable. That voice is unmistakable.":"audio/7c7ff8d082c5f382.mp3","gb-male\u0001to see someone live. I saw Seal live once.":"audio/cbd6d080d6c53caa.mp3","gb-male\u0001live show / gig. It was an amazing live show.":"audio/7197b6d3d3a051d3.mp3","gb-male\u0001crowd. The whole crowd was singing.":"audio/2e6a953fca4f9b35.mp3","gb-male\u0001to sing along. Everyone sang along.":"audio/ee3a7beb7d925dc4.mp3","gb-male\u0001goosebumps. That song gives me goosebumps.":"audio/a557fb22f9eb2d1f.mp3","gb-male\u0001lyrics. The lyrics are beautiful.":"audio/a7821964c0cd4234.mp3","gb-male\u0001tune / track. That's my favourite track.":"audio/1d26fb4ae710e072.mp3","gb-male\u0001catchy. The chorus is so catchy.":"audio/6d96139ca732f122.mp3","gb-male\u0001to be on tour. He's on tour this year.":"audio/60781c6ca762c4c4.mp3","gb-male\u0001soundtrack of my life. Seal is the soundtrack of my life.":"audio/2fee937b0f959ff8.mp3","gb-male\u0001Eu pergunto a alguém que tipo de música ela curte.":"audio/18a393013691ac31.mp3","gb-male\u0001Eu digo que sou fã de um artista e por quê.":"audio/9fce5be5c646159e.mp3","gb-male\u0001Eu descrevo um show: a plateia, cantar junto, os arrepios.":"audio/b34e08add591d722.mp3","gb-male\u0001Eu uso a música para criar vínculo com um cliente internacional.":"audio/5f16eb097c13ccd1.mp3","us-male\u0001We're gonna circle back on that and we'll confirm by Friday.":"audio/2274593410c391e4.mp3","us-female\u0001Você disse em entrevista: \"a língua trava, a palavra está na cabeça e não sai\". O bloco de Survival existe pra resolver exatamente isso. Começamos pelo cumprimento. Formal (primeiro contato, executivos): \"Good morning. It's a pleasure to meet you.\" Casual (gente que você já conhece): \"Hi! How's it going?\" Saber ler o registro certo é metade do jogo. A outra metade é simplesmente abrir a boca.":"audio/272e103902973948.mp3","us-female\u0001Good morning, it's a pleasure to meet you. I'm José Mário, contract manager here at Racional. Thank you for coming all the way to São Paulo. How was your flight?":"audio/79fee66ee708d2fd.mp3","us-female\u0001Pense no seu próximo encontro com alguém da Microsoft. É formal ou casual? Cumprimente em voz alta do jeito certo.":"audio/cd965e1fe33ed5b6.mp3","us-female\u0001Good morning. Good morning, it's a pleasure to meet you.":"audio/2b1f6d094ebec99f.mp3","us-female\u0001It's a pleasure to meet you. It's a pleasure to meet you.":"audio/371facfc54bd5392.mp3","us-female\u0001How's it going?. Hey, how's it going?":"audio/a41f3ff558dd2c2a.mp3","us-female\u0001contract manager. I'm the contract manager here.":"audio/72794ea8666ce336.mp3","us-female\u0001to introduce yourself. Let me introduce myself.":"audio/22aeedab6c66c018.mp3","us-female\u0001first encounter. This is our first encounter.":"audio/997e6322bc62d2f2.mp3","us-female\u0001formal. Use a formal greeting at first.":"audio/b0e6039db075647c.mp3","us-female\u0001casual. Later you can be more casual.":"audio/87b4c46e4c7cabff.mp3","us-female\u0001to shake hands. They shook hands and smiled.":"audio/3a313b7c2af00b92.mp3","us-female\u0001How was your flight?. How was your flight?":"audio/b723a3d96348bd33.mp3","us-female\u0001all the way. Thanks for coming all the way here.":"audio/bd3a331bbcb8d36d.mp3","us-female\u0001Welcome to São Paulo. Welcome to São Paulo!":"audio/11c5f11dc6761870.mp3","us-female\u0001Nice to meet you too. Nice to meet you too.":"audio/f90812b94b3ecfbb.mp3","us-female\u0001Please, have a seat. Please, have a seat.":"audio/26e6ecb5d54f3b65.mp3","us-female\u0001Can I get you a coffee?. Can I get you a coffee?":"audio/43ccafbea1cfd11f.mp3","us-female\u0001Likewise. Nice to meet you. — Likewise!":"audio/d6492ea44506e011.mp3","us-female\u0001to look forward to. I look forward to working with you.":"audio/324b55a834716098.mp3","us-female\u0001small talk. We had some small talk before the meeting.":"audio/b305a88766867832.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu cumprimento no registro certo — formal ou casual.":"audio/d751e1b43b2f695a.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu me apresento dizendo meu nome e cargo em inglês.":"audio/d885f22ad51ea6e8.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu faço small talk de abertura (How was your flight?).":"audio/ec5b5f595d527900.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu destravei a fala: a palavra saiu.":"audio/0e8f64a2c0b2027c.mp3","us-female\u0001Você trouxe isso na entrevista: como gerente de contratos, você fica no meio de dois especialistas — por exemplo, o gerente de instalações e o de comissionamento — que discordam. Você nem sempre manda tecnicamente neles, mas precisa decidir . São três passos: (1) reconhecer os dois lados com justiça, (2) dizer o critério que vai decidir (prazo, custo, risco, o cliente) e (3) bater o martelo e alinhar todo mundo no próximo passo. A linguagem neutra é tudo aqui.":"audio/5b17524a33cb6c6b.mp3","us-female\u0001I hear both of you. Marco, your concern about the schedule is valid. Ana, your point about test integrity is non-negotiable for the client. Given the risk to the Microsoft handover, here's my call: we hold the date and add one night shift. Let's align on that and move on.":"audio/b9d1bb7095f65b14.mp3","us-female\u0001Pense numa discordância real entre dois dos seus especialistas. Que critério deixaria você decidir de forma neutra? Responda — pode misturar inglês e português.":"audio/e79c5ae4f64e9cdd.mp3","us-female\u0001to mediate. I mediate between the two managers.":"audio/be762ec9dc01518f.mp3","us-female\u0001the deciding vote. I have to cast the deciding vote.":"audio/d1ecbd5bf467ebdb.mp3","us-female\u0001to cast a vote. Let me cast my vote.":"audio/be4cde750b406282.mp3","us-female\u0001I hear both of you. I hear both of you on this.":"audio/99af7999e46d3ddf.mp3","us-female\u0001valid. Your concern is valid.":"audio/d68a6647d42d6054.mp3","us-female\u0001non-negotiable. Test integrity is non-negotiable.":"audio/3f46785b47b07f2e.mp3","us-female\u0001to weigh up. Let me weigh up both options.":"audio/d9f4f0811d2af455.mp3","us-female\u0001criterion. The deciding criterion is risk.":"audio/5c9f161a2f79e13b.mp3","us-female\u0001trade-off. Every option has a trade-off.":"audio/47140c227847056e.mp3","us-female\u0001to make the call. Here's my call.":"audio/3590b12368700f3b.mp3","us-female\u0001to align on. Let's align on the next step.":"audio/fd9bafc97d37eb6f.mp3","us-female\u0001common ground. Let's find common ground.":"audio/7d08f978812ccbad.mp3","us-female\u0001to defer to. On safety, I defer to HSE.":"audio/3e9699908fb505b4.mp3","us-female\u0001for the record. For the record, this is my decision.":"audio/38f3f66316f6500e.mp3","us-female\u0001to move on. Let's align and move on.":"audio/6f35be62dd20bb5c.mp3","us-female\u0001to broker an agreement. I brokered an agreement between the two teams.":"audio/cb86356aa68f8261.mp3","us-female\u0001impartial. A mediator must stay impartial.":"audio/f2fe8bcc7b78659f.mp3","us-female\u0001to take ownership. Each manager takes ownership of the outcome.":"audio/63461a741f57127c.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu reconheço os dois lados de uma disputa técnica com justiça.":"audio/c89892a02013d94e.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu digo o critério que guia a minha decisão.":"audio/d2a2d463d4aa058f.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu dou o voto de minerva de forma clara e neutra.":"audio/3e8d24b4485768af.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu alinho todos no próximo passo e sigo em frente.":"audio/ee983ffb00b9bdb3.mp3","us-female\u0001Kindly share the update and we will revert to you by end of day.":"audio/5857eca52f1f90ec.mp3","us-female\u0001Esta é uma aula técnica — o vocabulário é mais denso de propósito, porque no seu dia a dia o cliente testa você justamente na parte de refrigeração (cooling). Vamos traduzir tudo. A CRAC (Computer Room Air Conditioner) tem o próprio compressor — ela resfria o ar localmente , como um ar-condicionado comum, porém industrial. A CRAH (Computer Room Air Handler) não tem compressor : ela usa água gelada (chilled water) que vem dos chillers e um ventilador empurra o ar por essa serpentina fria. As duas puxam o ar quente do corredor quente (hot aisle) , resfriam, e devolvem ar frio no corredor frio (cold aisle) , normalmente pelo piso elevado . O alvo é um setpoint (temperatura/umidade) e o sistema é projetado com redundância N+1 — sempre tem uma unidade reserva.":"audio/392ed4d2ef793b3c.mp3","us-female\u0001Each data hall runs on CRAH units fed by chilled water from the central plant. They draw return air from the hot aisle, cool it across the coil, and supply cold air to the cold aisle through the raised floor. We hold a 24-degree setpoint with N+1 redundancy on every row.":"audio/0d0fffdb35625fcc.mp3","us-female\u0001No seu projeto real, a refrigeração é DX (CRAC) ou água gelada (CRAH)? Explique a topologia e a redundância — pode misturar inglês e português no que travar.":"audio/1017f6807f1ac742.mp3","us-female\u0001CRAC. A CRAC has its own compressor.":"audio/44a2a4ecfe7d347b.mp3","us-female\u0001CRAH. The CRAH uses chilled water, not a compressor.":"audio/c17a64837c74be37.mp3","us-female\u0001chilled water. Chilled water is pumped to each CRAH.":"audio/f0c80d0770f52e06.mp3","us-female\u0001compressor. The CRAC's compressor failed during the test.":"audio/2ac3b21046213b49.mp3","us-female\u0001direct expansion (DX). A DX system cools the air directly.":"audio/a7b2c3a882cddf80.mp3","us-female\u0001setpoint. We hold a 24-degree setpoint.":"audio/721c051fcee9b703.mp3","us-female\u0001return air. Return air comes from the hot aisle.":"audio/72e35b89dfb4ab04.mp3","us-female\u0001supply air. Supply air goes to the cold aisle.":"audio/f39834755a2ef603.mp3","us-female\u0001raised floor. Cold air rises through the raised floor.":"audio/6b3664bb0a495569.mp3","us-female\u0001plenum. The underfloor plenum distributes the air.":"audio/12fec51901501c16.mp3","us-female\u0001hot aisle. Servers exhaust into the hot aisle.":"audio/032fa283520a2742.mp3","us-female\u0001cold aisle. Cold air is delivered to the cold aisle.":"audio/debe7996f007e095.mp3","us-female\u0001containment. Aisle containment improves efficiency.":"audio/a221416e6475f895.mp3","us-female\u0001humidity. We control temperature and humidity.":"audio/14a8940585012d18.mp3","us-female\u0001airflow. Each unit delivers a fixed airflow.":"audio/ff8983086b4100ab.mp3","us-female\u0001cooling capacity. Cooling capacity is measured in kW.":"audio/2e6181b575e1fadf.mp3","us-female\u0001heat load. The heat load rises with IT load.":"audio/2ab5a56c8498f5a5.mp3","us-female\u0001chiller. Chillers produce the chilled water.":"audio/43cd28b2c136b0c0.mp3","us-female\u0001N+1 redundancy. Every row has N+1 redundancy.":"audio/761af8539d907541.mp3","us-female\u0001fan. The fan pushes air across the coil.":"audio/7d87e7eb156e3509.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu sei explicar a diferença entre uma CRAC e uma CRAH.":"audio/ac60033de800d53c.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu descrevo o caminho do ar: return air, serpentina, supply air, piso elevado.":"audio/175b25cb3b93090a.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu falo de setpoint, umidade e redundância N+1 com precisão.":"audio/67ee612babb14424.mp3","us-female\u0001Eu conduzo o cliente pela topologia de refrigeração em inglês técnico.":"audio/1d474f3a25cb0cc6.mp3","gb-female\u0001Você disse claramente na entrevista: \"a primeira coisa que eu preciso fazer em toda reunião é contextualizar — explicar o motivo, o contexto, e só depois expor o trabalho\". Esse instinto é ouro. Esta aula te dá o inglês para isso. Uma abertura de contexto tem três batidas: background (onde estamos), purpose (por que estamos aqui) e roadmap (o que vamos cobrir). Com essas três, ninguém se perde.":"audio/a3c7378100ec622e.mp3","gb-female\u0001Thanks for joining, everyone. Quick context for those new to the call: we're building a hyperscale data center for AWS, and we're now in the electrical fit-out phase. The purpose today is to align on the energization milestone. I'll cover status, risks, and the decision we need from you.":"audio/38d5b9e81a133fd9.mp3","gb-female\u0001Lembre de uma reunião em que alguém se perdeu porque você foi direto ao detalhe. Como você prepararia o terreno na próxima? Responda — pode misturar inglês e português.":"audio/e367916e3c4d6d6d.mp3","gb-female\u0001to set the stage. Let me set the stage first.":"audio/1dd5f184e760e86a.mp3","gb-female\u0001context. Quick context for the new joiners.":"audio/c9199af2dfc047df.mp3","gb-female\u0001background. Some background on the project.":"audio/36c432c7612d8efb.mp3","gb-female\u0001purpose. The purpose of today is to align.":"audio/ca560025fde66e08.mp3","gb-female\u0001to align on. We need to align on the milestone.":"audio/45b9ac3065326552.mp3","gb-female\u0001to walk you through. I'll walk you through the status.":"audio/84965af36b01b178.mp3","gb-female\u0001for those new to…. For those new to the call…":"audio/96f89b31ac20a6ce.mp3","gb-female\u0001the big picture. Let me give you the big picture.":"audio/4dd6fec3cf7db57c.mp3","gb-female\u0001where we stand. Here's where we stand today.":"audio/1acc1b8024e6f935.mp3","gb-female\u0001to frame. Let me frame the problem.":"audio/79b5da1b803c57bb.mp3","gb-female\u0001milestone. The energization milestone is key.":"audio/6b6814952214933b.mp3","gb-female\u0001phase. We're in the fit-out phase.":"audio/bfd980e936efdd3f.mp3","gb-female\u0001roadmap. Here's the roadmap for today.":"audio/014d81941539e468.mp3","gb-female\u0001to recap. Let me quickly recap.":"audio/a67cf752641cd47b.mp3","gb-female\u0001the why before the what. Always give the why before the what.":"audio/64b0d0de1fedc718.mp3","gb-female\u0001Eu abro a reunião preparando o terreno (setting the stage).":"audio/08ee3ebb9f54dd0c.mp3","gb-female\u0001Eu dou o porquê e o contexto antes do quê.":"audio/5ec0973a49fbb265.mp3","gb-female\u0001Eu situo um novo stakeholder em uma frase.":"audio/bd442793b71aaae1.mp3","gb-female\u0001Eu apresento um roteiro: histórico, objetivo, decisão.":"audio/e9f877bc23a046af.mp3","us-female\u0001Let's go over the schedule and the next steps.":"audio/1a96b2badef93c05.mp3","gb-female\u0001Esta é uma aula BRIDGE , construída em torno do seu objetivo pessoal: um Executive MBA bilíngue . Ela oxigena os blocos técnicos com a linguagem da escola de negócios — começando por como as empresas são estruturadas e como as decisões são tomadas. Ideias-chave: o org chart (organograma — quem se reporta a quem), decisão centralizada × descentralizada , e onde está a autoridade . É exatamente o vocabulário de uma sala de MBA — e de um steering committee da Amazon.":"audio/6a6abca53a2b8aa0.mp3","gb-female\u0001On this project, decision-making is fairly decentralized. Each area manager owns their scope, but major change orders escalate to the steering committee. It keeps us fast on the ground without losing governance at the top.":"audio/876c10d34e925dba.mp3","gb-female\u0001Se você pudesse redesenhar a tomada de decisão do seu projeto para ser mais rápida, o que mudaria? Responda — pode misturar inglês e português.":"audio/7f707f1293a5cd54.mp3","gb-female\u0001organizational structure. Let's look at the organizational structure.":"audio/74cc6fa392852c22.mp3","gb-female\u0001org chart. The org chart shows who reports to whom.":"audio/640be291dc651a0e.mp3","gb-female\u0001to report to. Area managers report to me.":"audio/9ee6f7853a3b681d.mp3","gb-female\u0001decision-making. Decision-making is decentralized here.":"audio/b7d83ac28276664a.mp3","gb-female\u0001centralized. A centralized model decides at the top.":"audio/34efbd7fc8d34f55.mp3","gb-female\u0001decentralized. We use a decentralized model.":"audio/1f559ecfd91bd7fe.mp3","gb-female\u0001authority. Who has authority to approve this?":"audio/b53cdb2f8eecf34f.mp3","gb-female\u0001to delegate. I delegate scope to each manager.":"audio/f3f91e7bbb64b5a0.mp3","gb-female\u0001chain of command. Respect the chain of command.":"audio/a74de8f0865d3969.mp3","gb-female\u0001to escalate. Major issues escalate to the committee.":"audio/15a02c2b1098000b.mp3","gb-female\u0001governance. Governance protects the client.":"audio/e969235ebb1d135f.mp3","gb-female\u0001stakeholder. Every stakeholder has a voice.":"audio/f2eefa251f68a70d.mp3","gb-female\u0001hierarchy. A flat hierarchy moves faster.":"audio/d5d8883411a9a5d2.mp3","gb-female\u0001span of control. My span of control is six managers.":"audio/7d7603a14b3ad592.mp3","gb-female\u0001accountability. Accountability sits with the owner.":"audio/ad2ff9b9f9fb4a38.mp3","gb-female\u0001Eu descrevo uma estrutura organizacional em inglês.":"audio/12804d19c4b948bb.mp3","gb-female\u0001Eu diferencio decisão centralizada e descentralizada.":"audio/727eadf3e9f770b8.mp3","gb-female\u0001Eu uso vocabulário de MBA: governance, authority, escalate.":"audio/77965ecc4b7cb824.mp3","gb-female\u0001Eu conecto o meu trabalho às discussões de Executive MBA.":"audio/6cc51e3146faf1a8.mp3","us-male\u0001A primeira reunião não começa pelos números — começa por quebrar o gelo com classe e mostrar que você conduz a conversa. Três movimentos: (1) small talk curto e profissional (\"How was your trip?\"), (2) abrir a pauta com uma WH-question (\"What would you like to cover today?\") e (3) confirmar entendimento com question tag (\"We have 30 minutes, right?\") ou clarificação (\"Just to make sure I understood...\"). Regra de ouro do executivo: quem faz a pergunta conduz a sala. Você não precisa de inglês perfeito — precisa de inglês que mantém o controle da reunião .":"audio/9db9a56f903fc190.mp3","us-male\u0001Good morning, James. Thanks for joining. How was your week? Great. So, what would you like to cover today? On our side, I'd like to align on the schedule and the safety plan. We have about forty minutes, right? Perfect. Just to make sure I understood: you need the commissioning dates by Friday, correct?":"audio/6303939a6621a4d7.mp3","us-male\u0001Em 20 segundos, abra uma reunião com um cliente novo: cumprimente, faça um small talk e puxe a pauta com uma pergunta. Diga em voz alta, sem texto na frente.":"audio/97713bad13b5da03.mp3","us-male\u0001to break the ice. A quick question about the weather breaks the ice.":"audio/a9b9654f14748053.mp3","us-male\u0001How was your trip?. How was your trip to São Paulo?":"audio/9105dd19a6345a56.mp3","us-male\u0001to align on. Let's align on the schedule first.":"audio/73aae2410e011379.mp3","us-male\u0001agenda. What's on the agenda for today?":"audio/878dc92aacf7eab8.mp3","us-male\u0001to cover. What would you like to cover today?":"audio/e14c58f665d45043.mp3","us-male\u0001on our side. On our side, the main topic is safety.":"audio/f9e67bc282a00648.mp3","us-male\u0001to make sure. Just to make sure I understood you.":"audio/7725617e0655cd17.mp3","us-male\u0001right?. We have forty minutes, right?":"audio/4b9a6ab31ad8c1c7.mp3","us-male\u0001correct?. The deadline is Friday, correct?":"audio/30ee0e0ee8066977.mp3","us-male\u0001Could you clarify...?. Could you clarify the next step?":"audio/104a76f9dda846aa.mp3","us-male\u0001to move on. Let's move on to the budget.":"audio/e3c097870190e452.mp3","us-male\u0001to wrap up. Let's wrap up with the action items.":"audio/a52fdcbb318774ee.mp3","us-male\u0001action item. The first action item is the safety report.":"audio/f05e65eb0fb7872a.mp3","us-male\u0001to follow up. I'll follow up by email tomorrow.":"audio/bf49ad9c30671182.mp3","us-male\u0001I can open a meeting with short, professional small talk.":"audio/6e9af89b252ba5d1.mp3","us-male\u0001I can ask what the client wants to cover using a WH-question.":"audio/a35f669b899bf428.mp3","us-male\u0001I can confirm details with a question tag like 'right?' or 'correct?'.":"audio/d544452fcaadb7d5.mp3","us-male\u0001I can clarify what I heard with 'Just to make sure I understood...'.":"audio/ad6efae0365df297.mp3","us-male\u0001Em inglês, número falado tem armadilhas que travam executivos brasileiros. Vamos desarmá-las. Grandes números não levam 's': diz-se \"two billion\" , nunca \"two billions\". O 's' só aparece em expressões vagas: \"millions of dollars\" . Datas: americano fala \"May fifth\" ou \"the fifth of May\" ; o ano 2026 é \"twenty twenty-six\" . Moeda: \"R$1 billion\" = \"one billion reais\" ; \"US$2.5M\" = \"two point five million dollars\" . Durações: \"a 24-month project\" (com hífen, mês no singular quando vira adjetivo). Regra de ouro: número dito devagar e certo passa mais credibilidade que número dito rápido e errado.":"audio/4ac0a7d1bb997e23.mp3","us-male\u0001The total contract is worth two point five billion reais. We delivered the first phase in twenty twenty-five, and the full project runs for twenty-four months. Our safety record is strong: zero lost-time incidents in over three million working hours.":"audio/5e2cb4430574c0f3.mp3","us-male\u0001Em voz alta, diga três números do seu dia a dia em inglês: um valor em bilhões, um prazo em meses e um ano. Sem texto na frente.":"audio/bf2628d8fd9e2c02.mp3","us-male\u0001million. The budget is fifty million reais.":"audio/b6089555e130294a.mp3","us-male\u0001billion. The contract is worth two billion reais.":"audio/2b6089b8f3e074b2.mp3","us-male\u0001point (decimal). Two point five million, not two comma five.":"audio/c0fc1830c4f63dd7.mp3","us-male\u0001to be worth. The deal is worth one billion reais.":"audio/6683a32748079f6b.mp3","us-male\u0001figure. Let me walk you through the figures.":"audio/0095932c39622328.mp3","us-male\u0001percent. We cut costs by twelve percent.":"audio/f1b81bb8ef31092d.mp3","us-male\u0001deadline. The deadline is March thirty-first.":"audio/bde3e7ffd5db3cce.mp3","us-male\u0001duration. The duration is twenty-four months.":"audio/37b5881a5e517ce9.mp3","us-male\u0001a 24-month project. It's a twenty-four-month project.":"audio/7f1d390b8c5e6fab.mp3","us-male\u0001by (a date). We deliver by December.":"audio/b671ba9517661d85.mp3","us-male\u0001within. We finish within eighteen months.":"audio/b54dce1edf720bc1.mp3","us-male\u0001quarter. We report every quarter.":"audio/7bc309bd9cc73556.mp3","us-male\u0001year-on-year. Revenue grew year-on-year.":"audio/fccfb0c74d890182.mp3","us-male\u0001rough estimate. As a rough estimate, around forty million.":"audio/21cea8b053046067.mp3","us-male\u0001I can say large numbers without adding an 's' (two billion, not two billions).":"audio/b57f7ea701c6ca3e.mp3","us-male\u0001I can read decimals with 'point' and dates as ordinals.":"audio/5b09ca37bd227f92.mp3","us-male\u0001I can express a duration as an adjective ('a 24-month project').":"audio/c89a9cae3bfc6b86.mp3","us-male\u0001I can state a contract value and a deadline clearly and slowly.":"audio/870c274b520d336e.mp3","us-male\u0001Saber o número é uma coisa; dizê-lo numa negociação, sem gaguejar, é outra. Esta aula é treino de fluência sob pressão. Três frases-âncora que carregam qualquer número: (1) \"The total investment is around...\" (apresenta o valor), (2) \"We can deliver within...\" (compromisso de prazo) e (3) \"That gives us a buffer of...\" (margem de segurança). Dica executiva: ao dar um número sensível, baixe um pouco o ritmo e use um hedge (\"approximately\", \"around\", \"in the region of\") — soa confiante e te protege de cravar um valor exato cedo demais.":"audio/b746fd6008fa485d.mp3","us-male\u0001So, what are we looking at in terms of investment? The total is in the region of one point eight billion reais. And the timeline? We can deliver the full data center within twenty-two months, with a buffer of two months for commissioning. That keeps us comfortably on schedule.":"audio/3b24353639cb5351.mp3","us-male\u0001Imagine que um cliente acabou de perguntar o valor e o prazo do seu maior projeto. Responda em voz alta, em 20 segundos, usando um hedge no valor e uma margem no prazo. Sem texto na frente.":"audio/e6e308b50fc19876.mp3","us-male\u0001investment. The total investment is around one billion.":"audio/714f3d10de77acc5.mp3","us-male\u0001in the region of. In the region of two billion reais.":"audio/1418c1251628092d.mp3","us-male\u0001approximately. Approximately eighteen months.":"audio/f2e6fce43e2d90ff.mp3","us-male\u0001timeline. What's the timeline for delivery?":"audio/ee205b93dfbd3e24.mp3","us-male\u0001to deliver within. We deliver within twenty-four months.":"audio/947086315b934159.mp3","us-male\u0001buffer. We keep a buffer of two months.":"audio/f2f96fb79eab3f45.mp3","us-male\u0001on schedule. The project is on schedule.":"audio/1c4a581cc67026b7.mp3","us-male\u0001ahead of schedule. We finished ahead of schedule.":"audio/f5fe1be3e4a01bc6.mp3","us-male\u0001to commit to. We commit to the December deadline.":"audio/c218e9c66aa53e58.mp3","us-male\u0001ballpark. Give me a ballpark figure.":"audio/4f82c6f0d0a8080c.mp3","us-male\u0001upfront. Twenty percent is paid upfront.":"audio/5a0dc562422d44cc.mp3","us-male\u0001in installments. The rest is paid in installments.":"audio/dee8942e1981c328.mp3","us-male\u0001to come in under budget. We came in under budget last year.":"audio/96bf65d2f6afc55c.mp3","us-male\u0001milestone. Each milestone has a payment.":"audio/46efb194fbf4a57a.mp3","us-male\u0001I can present a contract value with a professional hedge ('in the region of').":"audio/df2d128ce5ccb08d.mp3","us-male\u0001I can commit to a deadline using 'within' and 'deliver'.":"audio/82ae8e72268bf3bf.mp3","us-male\u0001I can mention a safety buffer to sound like an experienced manager.":"audio/cee9ecca57b820e9.mp3","us-male\u0001I can answer a value-and-timeline question without freezing.":"audio/74a4aa52ddd8814b.mp3"}